# Install devDependencies even when NODE_ENV=production.
#
# The Angular CLI, `@angular/build` and TypeScript are all devDependencies — everything the build
# needs. If the host installs with NODE_ENV=production, npm omits them and `ng build` fails with a
# missing-binary error that says nothing about the cause.
#
# This is the same failure that broke the API's first two deploys on Render, where NODE_ENV had to
# be `production` for the auth cookie and npm read it during install. Vercel does normally install
# devDependencies, so this is precaution rather than a fix for something observed — but it costs
# nothing, and the failure it prevents is one we have already paid for once.
#
# In the repository rather than in a platform setting on purpose: a build command configured in a
# dashboard is frozen at project creation and does not follow the code. That is precisely how the
# Render fix missed the first time.
include=dev
